/* settings.def -- every configuration key this host reads, once.
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT.  Copyright (c) 2026 VCThunder contributors.
 *
 * ONE table, three consumers: config.c builds both its defaults and its parser
 * from it, launcher.c builds its catalogue from it, and
 * tools/check-launcher-settings.py holds it against the shipped vcthunder.ini.
 * Nothing else may carry a second copy of any column here: that is the whole
 * point of the file. src/settings.h carries the row's shape and says why one
 * table is the only arrangement that can be held to itself.
 *
 *      SETTING(section, key, STORE(...), SHOW(...))
 *          A key the shipped ini carries and the launcher edits. The checker
 *          requires exactly one of these per shipped key and vice versa.
 *
 *      SETTING_DEV(section, key, STORE(...))
 *          A developer switch: parsed, never shown, and deliberately absent
 *          from the shipped file (docs/configuration.md §6).
 *
 *      STORE(kind, field, default, choices, min, max)
 *          `field` is a member of shim_config_t. The DEFAULT IS INI TEXT and
 *          is parsed by the same code the file goes through, so a default that
 *          could not be written in the file cannot exist.
 *
 *      STORE_ELSEWHERE(default, choices, min, max)
 *          diego.c, dinput.c and input_probe.c read [analog], [ffb] and the
 *          binding sections from the file themselves, through their own
 *          section-precedence rule. config.c must not touch those keys; the
 *          launcher still edits them and the ini still ships them.
 *
 * `section` is the CANONICAL section. config.c accepts a known key found in
 * another section too, because docs/configuration.md §6 promises exactly that
 * ("the parser takes any key it knows, wherever it finds it"), but it now
 * says so in the log instead of silently. That fallback needs key names to be
 * unique across sections, which the checker enforces.
 */


/* ---- PAGE_GRAPHICS: the picture. [graphics] ---------------------------- */
